How maul runs it: {{if eq .Form "http"}}each step sends its request to the named component of the running preview,
in order, and fails the check unless the response matches its `expect`; `capture` keeps a value from a response for
later steps.{{else if eq .Form "browser"}}the steps run in order in a fresh browser on the running preview, its
window always {{.Viewport.Width}} by {{.Viewport.Height}} CSS pixels, each an action or an assertion; `visible` means a
person can see the element, `legible` that a person can read its text, and `clickable` that it, not something covering
